            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0245" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4778: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-03T10:00:00+01:00">July 3, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 3—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>280. 1. Requesting consideration at this Assembly, Ethiopia has presented two
                    draft resolutions<anchor n="1" xml:id="d178-f1"/> to the following effect: <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Categorical nonrecognition of any annexation obtained by force.</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Financial assistance in the form of a loan of 10,000,000 pounds
                            sterling to be issued Ethiopia and guaranteed by League members.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>2. The general formal position of the Ethiopian delegation here, presented in
                    other communications, is that the Italians have not effectively occupied more
                    than a half of their territory and that the Ethiopian Government remains in full
                        <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">de
                        jure</hi> existence.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
